  "checks": {
    "identity-and-scale": "All eight exported poses and controlled-clock live camp frames reviewed. Same bald Elder, white braided beard, olive embroidered coat, pouches and boots. Standing-equivalent seated placement uses the existing source-bound render calibration; no walking scale or direction continuity approval.",
    "station-and-foot-contact": "Fixed camp root, seated pelvis, stool and both boots retain the seated ground baseline through0-7. The crack inspection includes its painted wooden table in the combined fixed-view reference; it is not an independent workstation. No moving sole/cane calibration is claimed.",
    "hand-and-tool-contact": "Left hand supports the wood below the metal eye while right hand examines the metal crack. Raised0/1/7, lowered3/4 and tilted5/6 retain the same visible grip and one connected head/handle. Right index can release to point; the supporting left hand remains on the handle. No hidden grip or 3D rigidity measurement is claimed.",
    "prop-continuity": "One pickaxe with straight wooden handle, one metal eye/head and the same Elder/stool throughout all eight poses. Crack inspection table is a combined painted prop. No released item, inventory output, duplication or repair result is awarded.",
    "completion-and-reset": "Actual controlled-clock camp renderer exposed0-7 at unchanged125ms timings, one completion and terminal7 hold. Sequence advances after held completion when the next atlas is ready, then final action stays held. Departure removes work state. Continuous7-to0 replay and seamless transitions between different camp activities are unapproved."
